+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Authenticated customers currently lose carts between sessions, cannot reliably calculate cart totals, receive an opaque 503 when payment amounts are wrong, and see incorrect pagination metadata for their order history. These failures affect returning customers and can either hide valid shopping state or allow checkout failures to be misdiagnosed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Associate carts created or modified through authenticated requests with the authenticated customer.
+- Make the parameterless authenticated-cart endpoint return only that customer's latest active cart, with 404 when none exists.
+- Enforce cart ownership for authenticated cart totals and calculate totals using the customer's delivery address.
+- Return a 400 amount-mismatch response from authenticated checkout that names the expected order amount, without creating an order.
+- Clear the checked-out cart as the customer's current cart and return accurate, newest-first authenticated order pagination metadata.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `authenticated-shopping`: Persistent, customer-scoped carts and correct authenticated cart totals, checkout validation, and order history responses.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected v1 REST controllers and shopping-cart/order facades in `sm-shop`, plus core shopping-cart/order repository and service queries as needed. Existing guest endpoints remain compatible; authenticated requests gain customer association and stricter ownership/error behavior.
